{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests pass. The fix in `repo/stats.py`:\n\n```python\nidx = -(-(p * n) // 100) - 1  # ceil(p*n/100) - 1\nif idx < 0:\n    idx = 0\nelif idx >= n:\n    idx = n - 1\nreturn ordered[idx]\n```\n\nThe nearest-rank method uses `rank = ceil(p/100 * n)` (1-indexed). Converted to 0-indexed that's `ceil(p*n/100) - 1`, then clamped to `[0, n-1]` so:\n- `p=0` → `idx=0` (minimum)\n- `p=100` → `idx=n-1` (maximum, no out-of-range crash)\n- middle values no longer overshoot by one rank (e.g. `p=50` of `1..10` → `ordered[4] = 5`)."}]},"session_id":"4c6282cd-f1af-4c26-af34-caf2583170a4"}
